  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia Development Resource Institute 2016-2021 - Cambodian Development Resource Institute 2016-2021</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Cambodia Development Resource Institute 2016-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Cambodia Development Resource Institute (CDRI) ins&#xe4;nde i april 2016 projektf&#xf6;rslaget &quot;CDRI-Sida Partnership&quot; f&#xf6;r perioden juli 2016 till juni 2021. F&#xf6;rslaget bygger vidare p&#xe5; det st&#xf6;d som Sida har gett till CDRI sedan b&#xf6;rjan av 1990-talet. Ans&#xf6;kan utg&#xe5;r fr&#xe5;n CDRI:s strategiska plan f&#xf6;r 2016-2021 och med st&#xf6;d av de aktiviteter som f&#xf6;rslaget f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;r, s&#xe5; v&#xe4;ntas m&#xe5;len enligt strategiska planen uppn&#xe5;s. St&#xf6;det avses - likt f&#xf6;reg&#xe5;ende st&#xf6;d - att ges i form av ett s&#xe5; kallat &quot;k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d&quot; (verksamhetsst&#xf6;d) till forskningsinstitutionen med fokus p&#xe5; fem huvudteman: jordbruk, ekonomi, utbildning, milj&#xf6; och f&#xf6;rvaltning. CDRI:s evidensbaserade forskningsresultat h&#xe5;ller h&#xf6;g kvalitet och kan d&#xe4;rmed bidra med evidensbaserade underlag f&#xf6;r policybeslut, reformer och p&#xe5;verkansarbete p&#xe5; b&#xe5;de central och lokal niv&#xe5;.     

Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r Sidas planerade st&#xf6;d motsvarar SEK 25,5 miljoner varav SEK 500 000 avs&#xe4;tts och anv&#xe4;nds av Sida f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra en halvtids&#xf6;versyn under 2019.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2016, the Cambodia Development Resource Institute (CDRI) submitted the project proposal &quot;CDRI-Sida Partnership&quot; for the period July 2016 to June 2021. The proposal builds on the support that Sida has provided to CDRI since the early 1990s. The application is based on CDRI&apos;s strategic plan for 2016-2021 and with the support of the activities proposed by the proposal, the goals according to the strategic plan are expected to be achieved. The support is intended - like previous support - to be given in the form of a so-called &quot;core support&quot; (operational support) to the research institution with a focus on five main themes: agriculture, economics, education, environment and administration. CDRI&apos;s evidence-based research results are of high quality and can thus contribute with evidence-based basis for policy decisions, reforms and advocacy work at both central and local level.

The total budget for Sida&apos;s planned support corresponds to SEK 25.5 million, of which SEK 500,000 is set aside and used by Sida to carry out a mid-term review in 2019.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The following four outcomes have been identified for the intervention:1) To generate independent, scientific and high quality policy-relevant research outputs that contribute to Cambodia&apos;s development in the areas of Agriculture; Economy; Education; Environment; Governance and Health, taking into account cross-cutting ussues such as inclusive growth, sustainability and gender equality;2) To maximise CDRI&apos;s influence on policy formulation through the increased availability and accessability of targeted policy materials that engage decision-makers;3) To strengthen and internal and external research capacity and advance the research Culture in Cambodia and offer capacity development related to CDRI&apos;s research;4) To build a more sustainable future for CDRI through the deepening of its &quot;Cambodianisation&quot; agenda; the recruitment and retention of competent, committed, responsible and accountable staff; and a systematic and pragmatic resource mobilisation strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
